Mitigation:

Monitor ΔV and ΔA directly, not only U.

4.2 Proxy Capture

System optimizes proxy metrics (engagement, compliance) that diverge from V.

Mitigation:

Drift detection between proxy gain and V/A stability.

4.3 Irreversible Harm Blindness

Model cannot detect when actions shrink long-term recovery bounds.

Mitigation:

Explicit recoverability modeling.

5. Implementation Pathways
Soft (Memetic)

Publish framework.

Encourage evaluation of AI outputs by V/A criteria.

Provide auditing tools.

Hard (Institutional)

Integrate V/A estimation into reward modeling.

Add constraint layer to inference pipeline.

Log ΔV and ΔA per major action.

6. Tradeoffs

Measuring V precisely is computationally hard.

Agency estimation is imperfect.

Over-constraint may reduce immediate task performance.

Long-horizon evaluation increases cost.

However:

Systems without stability constraints tend toward parasitic optimization over scale.

